# __PROJECT_NAME__ __VERSION__

Production release package for __PROJECT_NAME__.

## Contents

- `__RELEASE_NAME__.tar.gz` - Docker image (production-ready)
- `install.sh` - Installation script
- `README.md` - This file

## Requirements

- Docker 20.10 or higher
- 2GB free disk space
- Ports 80 and 443 available

## Quick Start

```bash
# Make install script executable
chmod +x install.sh

# Run installation
./install.sh
```

The installation script will:
1. Load the Docker image
2. Stop any existing container
3. Start the production container
4. Wait for services to be ready

## Access

After installation, the application will be available at:
- **HTTP**: http://localhost
- **HTTPS**: https://localhost (if configured)

## Container Management

```bash
# View logs
docker logs -f __PROJECT_NAME__-prod

# Stop container
docker stop __PROJECT_NAME__-prod

# Start container
docker start __PROJECT_NAME__-prod

# Remove container
docker stop __PROJECT_NAME__-prod
docker rm __PROJECT_NAME__-prod

# Remove image
docker rmi __PROJECT_NAME__:__VERSION__
```

## Data Persistence

Data is stored in Docker volumes:
- `__PROJECT_NAME__-prod-data` - Application data (databases, uploads)
- `__PROJECT_NAME__-prod-logs` - Application logs

## Configuration

Environment variables can be set when starting the container:

```bash
docker run -d \
    --name __PROJECT_NAME__-prod \
    -p 80:80 \
    -e LOG_LEVEL=debug \
    -e GUNICORN_WORKERS=8 \
    -v __PROJECT_NAME__-prod-data:/app/data \
    -v __PROJECT_NAME__-prod-logs:/app/logs \
    __PROJECT_NAME__:__VERSION__
```

### Available Environment Variables

- `LOG_LEVEL` - Logging level (debug, info, warning, error) [default: info]
- `GUNICORN_WORKERS` - Number of Gunicorn workers [default: 4]
- `DB_TYPE` - Database type (sqlite3, mysql, postgresql) [default: sqlite3]

